       <t indent="0" pn="section-22-2">The threat to DHCP is inherently an insider threat (assuming a
 properly configured network where DHCP ports are blocked on the
 perimeter gateways of the enterprise).  Regardless of the gateway
@@ -6332,14 +5977,14 @@
 attack would cause all network communication from the client to fail.</t>
       <t indent="0" pn="section-22-5">A malicious DHCP server might cause a client to set its SOL_MAX_RT
